  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen LP in apparel industry CCAWDU</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coalition of Cambodian Apparel Workers Democratic Union (C.CAWDU) has been engaged in this proposal development since it started due to its relevancy and expertise. C.CAWDU is an independent national federation of trade unions in the garment sector of Cambodia. It is a member of the Board of the NSSF and a number of tripartite mechanisms at national level. C.CAWDU has witnessed remarkable growth since it was set up in 2000.  Since then, C.CAWDU has established as a respected independent trade union serving a growing number of members and is recognized by external stakeholders and the government as a credible, legitimate labour organisation. In April 2006, C.CAWDU played a central role in the establishment of the Cambodian Labour Confederation (CLC), registered with the MoLVT underthe registration number 1587 KB/VK on 31 December 2008. Together with CLC, C.CAWDU has lobbied the government on a regular basis toprovide health and work accident insurance and pensions for workers. Over the years, C.CAWDU has contributed significantly towards improving working conditions and living standards for workers in the garment industry. And C.CAWDU has won the Arthur Svensson International Prize in 2012 for Trade Union Rights for their persistent work in grassroots struggle and mass mobilisation for better pay and improved working conditions in the clothing industry in the Kingdom.

C.CAWDU is one of the strongest garment workers&#x2019; federations in Asia, and despite a harsh environment for trade union work, will continue to:
&#xf0d8; Support mobilisation, facilitating dialogue and peaceful strikes and rallies
&#xf0d8; Provide training and education to their members
&#xf0d8; Negotiate collective agreements with factories and employers
&#xf0d8; Provide legal redress on urgent appeal proceduresfor workers
&#xf0d8; Participate in social policy dialogue on key reforms inrelation to garment sector</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coalition of Cambodian Apparel Work</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coalition of Cambodian Apparel Workers Democratic Union (CCAWDU) is an independent federation established in 2000, has been organised more than 80,000 members from more than 60 local unions in garment and shoes factories. They are and focusing their workon strengthening local unions, training leaders, supporting dispute resolution and representing workers in different instances. CCAWDU have been in the front line for more than 15 years. Based on their strong grassroots concept, they have been also helping to create the Cambodian Labour Confederation (CLC), the member of a tripartite bodyLabour Advisory Committee (LAC), a decision body on minimum wage for garment industry, and a board member of the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) the body that in charge of worker#s health insurance. They continue fighting for better working and living conditions of worker in Phnom Penh and other provinces (Kandal, Kampong Spue, Kampong Som, Kampong Chhang, SvayReing, Preyveng,Takeo) and to get informal sector workersincluded in NSSF.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
